; MX3 (part 3) the 0F page (docs/v35s-mechanisms.md section 3.4; README "MX3 (part 3)").
; The E word pops the second opcode byte with the 0F opcode (into the ModR/M register, as a
; ModR/M form's E word pops its ModR/M byte: the frozen model's start takes the page's second
; byte, page_take=own) and the dispatch reads the second level on it (the decode's op3: the
; second byte's bits 3:1, the operation; w: the operand width). A form with a ModR/M byte pops
; it on its routine's first word, an EAC word: its mode decides the next word (register mode:
; the label, the register form's path; a memory mode: the EA head of the mode called, returning
; to the memory path's add; mod 00 without a head: the add). Every routine is the data book's
; formula first; a clock beyond it is a named act or an OPEN word declared "silicon longer than
; the book" with the run the frozen model is exact on. Clocks in the comments are from the E
; word that popped the 0F opcode (E + 0; the dispatch E + 1; the routine's first word E + 2).

; ---- the packed BCD strings: ADD4S / SUB4S (0F 20 / 22), CMP4S (0F 26). (CL + 1) / 2 byte
; pairs; the source byte at DS0:IX + i (a prefix's segment), read before the destination's at
; DS1:IY + i, the result written back (ADD4S / SUB4S). The loop counter is loaded by the first
; word from CL (CN_CLH: CL shifted right by one with its low bit as the carry-in); a zero count
; skips the loop. tmpc is the pair's offset i. Every request is posted with its address already
; in the address register; the destination's address moves on the source read's second clock
; (before any wait state: MX1g's BW law would hold a move under a wait state), the next pair's
; after the write's end. F after the write: the EU holds until the write's end (RAMEN = 1, the
; write may land in the registers' RAM: mechanisms 3.3).

routine add4s op=20,22 page=0f book="ADD4S" n=4 diff=1 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) ADD4S / SUB4S are a byte loop with no data-dependent exit (the qprobe add4s / sub4s runs, CL 1 2 4 8): a 13-word head with a bus-idle fourth word, ceil(CL / 2) iterations `Y D . . . U D . . . . . . Z D .` (read the source, read the destination, write the destination: 30 clocks at W = 0), a 10-word tail `. . . . . . . . N .`"
    ra=IX rb=CW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=TC s2=ZERO cnt=CLH alu=BCDI ; the source's address (IX + 0), the pair offset 0 into tmpc, the counter <- (CL + 1) / 2; the carry cleared, the zero term set
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) B: the head's bus-idle fourth word
    jc=CNTZ:a4_tail                         ; no byte pair: the flags
    open call=w7                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) eight words with no act (the head's 13) (the call and the shared delay's 7)
a4_pair: rl=x bi                            ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (the source's read posted three words later)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IY + i (the destination's address)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=BYTE               ; post the source byte's read (Y + 3)
    f d1=TA s1=OPR d2=ADDR s2=SIG           ; D: F: the source byte into tmpa; the destination's address into the address register (the read's datum taken)
    alu=ADD ax=TC ay=ONE                    ; SIGMA = i + 1
    d1=TC s1=SIG                            ; tmpc <- i + 1
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; U: post the destination byte's read (the datum + 5)
    f d1=TB s1=OPR                          ; D: F: the destination byte into tmpb
    alu=BCDS ax=TB ay=TA wid=BYTE           ; the BCD byte step (the add / the subtract by op3; the carry in and out, the zero term)
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG                          ; the result into the write datum
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IX + i + 1 (the next pair's source)
    open call=w3                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) four words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 3)
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; Z: post the write (the datum + 8)
    f d1=ADDR s1=SIG                        ; D: F: the write's end; the next source's address
    loop=a4_pair                            ; the counter step: the next pair
a4_tail: open call=w6                       ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) seven words with no act (the tail's ten) (the call and the shared delay's 6)
    alu=BCDF wf                             ; the flags: CY S AC the last carry, Z P the zero term, V 0
    e ro                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (N)

routine cmp4s op=26 page=0f book="CMP4S" n=4 diff=2 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) CMP4S is ADD4S's head, iterations `Y D . . . U D . . . . . . . .` (25 clocks at W = 0) and an 11-word tail (the qprobe cmp4s runs)"
    ra=IX rb=CW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA d2=TC s2=ZERO cnt=CLH alu=BCDI ; the source's address (IX + 0), the pair offset 0 into tmpc, the counter <- (CL + 1) / 2; the borrow cleared, the zero term set
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) B: the head's bus-idle fourth word
    jc=CNTZ:c4_tail                         ; no byte pair: the flags
    open call=w7                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) eight words with no act (the head's 13) (the call and the shared delay's 7)
c4_pair: rl=x bi                            ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (the source's read posted three words later)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IY + i (the destination's address)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP wid=BYTE               ; post the source byte's read (Y + 3)
    f d1=TA s1=OPR d2=ADDR s2=SIG           ; D: F: the source byte into tmpa; the destination's address
    alu=ADD ax=TC ay=ONE                    ; SIGMA = i + 1
    d1=TC s1=SIG                            ; tmpc <- i + 1
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1 wid=BYTE               ; U: post the destination byte's read (the datum + 5)
    f d1=TB s1=OPR                          ; D: F: the destination byte into tmpb
    alu=BCDS ax=TB ay=TA wid=BYTE           ; the BCD byte step (the subtract: the borrow and the zero term; nothing written)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=ADD ax=RA ay=TC      ; SIGMA = IX + i + 1 (the next pair's source)
    d1=ADDR s1=SIG                          ; the next source's address
    open call=w3                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) four words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 3)
    loop=c4_pair                            ; the counter step: the next pair
c4_tail: open call=w7                       ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) eight words with no act (the tail's eleven) (the call and the shared delay's 7)
    alu=BCDF wf                             ; the flags
    e ro                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (N)

; ---- the bit operations TEST1 / CLR1 / SET1 / NOT1 (0F 10-1F: op3 1:0 the operation, the
; width the second byte's bit 0, bit 3 an imm3 / imm4 index after the operand, else CL; the
; index modulo the width). The first word pops the ModR/M byte (EAC): a register operand goes
; to the register path (the operand and CL read on ports B and A, the bit operation, the write);
; a memory operand calls the EA head of its mode and returns to the add, the read, F with the
; bit operation, the write's post, E held to its end (RAMEN). The CL index is read into tmpb
; after the add; the imm index is popped after the read's issue (the frozen model's takes).
routine b1tcl op=10,11 page=0f ea=bare diff=r:0,m00:-1,d8:0,d16:0,dir:1 book="TEST1 reg8,CL" bookm="TEST1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: book error where the measured routine is shorter than the book (the qprobe shape below); silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) TEST1 mem,CL is `P . P . C Y DN .` (the qprobe t1wmcl runs): the add, the ModR/M byte released and CL into tmpb, a word with no act, the commit word C, the request word Y, the read (Y + 3), D with TEST1 and E; the register form `P . P . . CN .` (Q31)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1tcl_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head (the pops)
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    ra=CW d1=TB s1=RA rl=1                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word); CL (by the width) into tmpb: the bit index
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bi alt                                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C: the commit word (bus-idle, and held on the clock a back-to-back fetch starts)
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=TB wf e ro          ; D N: F: TEST1 on the datum at the bit CL names (S Z P; CY AC V cleared); E (TEST1 writes nothing)
b1tcl_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10, Q31) TEST1 r,CL is `P . P . . CN .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 10) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    e ro bi alt                             ; E: pop the next opcode; (qprobe round 10, B4) C N: the commit word (bus-idle, and held on the clock a back-to-back fetch starts); ro: released
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA wf      ; the word after E: the register and CL, TEST1's flags written (the write port's: MX3's WBR)

routine b1tim op=18,19 page=0f ea=bare diff=r:1,m00:0,d8:1,d16:1,dir:2 book="TEST1 reg8,imm3" bookm="TEST1 mem8,imm3" why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) TEST1 mem,imm is `P . PC Y DPN .` (the qprobe runs: 24 / 24): the add, the ModR/M byte's release on the commit word C, Y, the index popped under the wait and released on D; TEST1 r,imm `P . P . . CPN .` (the qprobe t1 r,imm runs): the CL form's with the index released on the commit word"
    pop=modrm eac=b1tim_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    rl=1 bi alt                             ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P C: the ModR/M byte released; the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the datum word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=IMM8 wf e ro rl=1   ; D P N: F: TEST1 on the datum at the bit the index names; the index released; E
b1tim_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) TEST1 r,imm is `P . P . . CPN .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the commit word)
    open d1=TB s1=IMM8                      ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act; (F5c) the index into tmpb (the next E pop's short displacement overwrites IL before the word after E)
    e ro bi alt rl=1                        ; E: pop the next opcode; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C P N: the commit word, the index and the next opcode released
    rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=TB wf            ; the word after E: the register and the index (tmpb), TEST1's flags written (the write port's: MX3's WBR)

routine b1ccl op=12,13 page=0f ea=bare diff=r:0,m00:1,d8:2,d16:2,dir:3 book="CLR1 reg8,CL" bookm="CLR1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) CLR1 mem,CL is `P . P . C Y D Z G N .` (the qprobe c1mcl runs): TEST1 mem,CL's head, D with CLR1, a word, Z (the write's post), G N; the register form `P . P . . CN . .` (Q31)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1ccl_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    ra=CW d1=TB s1=RA rl=1                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word); CL into tmpb: the bit index
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bi alt                                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C: the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=TB                  ; D: F: CLR1 on the datum
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG                          ; the result into the write datum ((qprobe round 12, Q38) the word before Z)
    bus=MEMW                                ; Z: post the write
    e ro bi                                 ; E: (qprobe round 9, Q23) G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
b1ccl_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10, Q31) CLR1 r,CL is `P . P . . CN . .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 10) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    ro bi alt                               ; (qprobe round 10, B4) C N: the commit word (bus-idle, and held on the clock a back-to-back fetch starts); ro: the next opcode released
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA e       ; the register and CL: CLR1; E (the E row's operation, a register form's; one word after the release)
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

routine b1cim op=1A,1B page=0f ea=bare diff=r:1,m00:2,d8:3,d16:3,dir:4 book="CLR1 reg8,imm3" bookm="CLR1 mem8,imm3" why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) CLR1 r,imm is `P . P . . CPN . .` (the qprobe c1i runs); CLR1 mem,imm by analogy (not probed: kept only while the corpus rows confirm it, spec 8 D) SET1 mem,imm's `P . PC Y DPZ G N .` with one word more before Z (as the CL forms)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1cim_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    rl=1 bi alt                             ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P C: the ModR/M byte released; the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the datum word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=IMM8 rl=1           ; D P: F: CLR1 on the datum; the index released
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG                          ; the result into the write datum (CLR1's word before Z, by analogy)
    bus=MEMW                                ; Z: post the write
    e ro bi                                 ; E: G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
b1cim_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) CLR1 r,imm is `P . P . . CPN . .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the commit word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    ro bi alt rl=1                          ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C P N: the commit word, the index and the next opcode released
    rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=IMM8 e           ; the register: CLR1; E (the E row's operation)
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

routine b1scl op=14,16 page=0f ea=bare diff=r:0,m00:1,d8:2,d16:2,dir:3 book="SET1 reg8,CL" bookm="SET1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) SET1 / NOT1 mem,CL is `P . P . C Y DZ G N .` (the qprobe n1mcl runs): TEST1 mem,CL's head, D with the operation, Z on the word after it, G N; the register form `P . P . . CN .` (Q31)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1scl_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
b1scl_m2: ra=CW d1=TB s1=RA rl=1            ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word); CL into tmpb: the bit index
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bi alt                                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C: the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=TB                  ; D: F: SET1 / NOT1 on the datum
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG bus=MEMW                 ; Z: the result into the write datum; post the write
    e ro bi                                 ; E: G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
b1scl_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10, Q31) SET1 / NOT1 r,CL is `P . P . . CN .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 10) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 10) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA e ro bi alt  ; the register and CL: SET1 / NOT1; E (the E row's operation, a register form's); (qprobe round 10, B4) C N: the commit word (bus-idle, held on the clock a back-to-back fetch starts); ro: released
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

routine b1sclw op=15,17 page=0f ea=bare diff=r:-1,m00:1,d8:2,d16:2,dir:3 book="SET1 reg8,CL" bookm="SET1 mem8,CL" why="OPEN: book error where the measured routine is shorter than the book (the qprobe shape below), silicon longer than the book on its other paths; (qprobe round 10) SET1 / NOT1 r16,CL (0F 15 / 17) keep the round-9 register routine: built as the byte forms' `P . P . . CN .` (Q31 measured on the byte forms) they lost nine corpus runs (F39 page-set1); (qprobe round 12, Q38) the memory forms are SET1 mem,CL's `P . P . C Y DZ G N .` (n1mcl measured on 0F 16)"
    pop=modrm eac=b1sclw_r                  ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX jmp=b1scl_m2     ; the EA's add; SET1 mem,CL's words (b1scl)
b1sclw_r: rl=1 open call=w2                 ; OPEN: 3 clocks: book clocks with no act (SET1 reg,CL 7) (the call and the shared delay's 2); the ModR/M byte released (the round-9 register path)
    ra=CW rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=RA e ro    ; the register and CL: SET1 / NOT1; E (the E row's operation, a register form's); ro: released
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

routine b1sim op=1C,1D,1E,1F page=0f ea=bare diff=r:1,m00:2,d8:3,d16:3,dir:4 book="SET1 reg8,imm3" bookm="SET1 mem8,imm3" why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) SET1 / NOT1 mem,imm is `P . PC Y DPZ G N .` (the qprobe s1mi runs) and r,imm `P . P . . CPN .` (the qprobe n1i runs): TEST1's heads, the write's post on the word after the datum"
    pop=modrm eac=b1sim_r                   ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    rl=1 bi alt                             ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P C: the ModR/M byte released; the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the datum word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    bus=MEMR                                ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f alu=BIT ax=OPR ay=IMM8 rl=1           ; D P: F: SET1 / NOT1 on the datum; the index released
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG bus=MEMW                 ; Z: the result into the write datum; post the write
    e ro bi                                 ; E: G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
b1sim_r: open                              ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) SET1 / NOT1 r,imm is `P . P . . CPN .`: the second word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    pop=il                                  ; pop the bit index (released on the commit word)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    rb=RM alu=BIT ax=RB ay=IMM8 e ro bi alt rl=1  ; the register: SET1 / NOT1; E; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C P N: the commit word, the index and the next opcode released
    wr=RM ws=SIG                            ; the register written on the word after E (its write port: MX3's WBR)

; ---- the digit rotates ROL4 / ROR4 (0F 28 / 2A: op3 0 / 1) on a byte register or at [m]
; with AL (the data book's and the V35's: AL's high digit kept). The register path is the
; book's length after the take sync's wait (the EAC word's ModR/M pop arms it: F32-push-ror4_dl-
; k1-pE-w2, the model exact, waits to the back-to-back fetch's delivery at E + 9, w0 at E + 5);
; the memory path the book's (ROL4) and ROR4 four more, as the register forms (the model's
; read's end to the write's issue 11 and 15: F32-out-rol4_m-k1-pE-w0, F32-out-ror4_m-k1-pE-w0).
; The result's write-back runs past E on the register path (the model's wb 2: an OUT imm8
; after it waits, MX1f).
routine rol4 op=28 page=0f ea=bare book="ROL4 reg8" bookm="ROL4 mem8" diff=r:1,m00:3,d8:4,d16:4,dir:5 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) ROL4 r8 is `P . P . . C`, ten words, `N .` (18; the qprobe rol4 runs) and ROL4 mem `P . PC Y D`, eight words, `Z G N .` (the qprobe rol4m runs): the 0F head, the commit word, the rotate on its fixed words (ROR4 four words more in both forms)"
    pop=modrm eac=r4l_r                     ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    rl=1 bi alt                             ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P C: the ModR/M byte released; the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR wid=BYTE                       ; post the byte's read (Y + 3)
    f ra=AW wid=BYTE alu=R4 ax=OPR ay=RA    ; D: F: the digit rotate of the datum with AL (SIGMA the byte, tmpc the new AL)
    wr=AW wid=BYTE ws=TC                    ; AL written
    open call=w7                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) eight words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 7)
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG bus=MEMW wid=BYTE        ; Z: the byte into the write datum; post the write (nine words after the datum: the model's eight)
    e ro bi                                 ; E: G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
r4l_r: open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bi alt                                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C: the commit word
    rb=RM ra=AW wid=BYTE alu=R4 ax=RB ay=RA ; the register and AL: the digit rotate
    wr=AW wid=BYTE ws=TC                    ; AL written
    wr=RM wid=BYTE ws=SIG                   ; the register written (F5b: after AL: with AL the operand, the operand's result stays, silicon f5r rot4al)
    open call=w6                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) seven words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 6)
    e ro                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (N: ten words after the commit word)

routine ror4 op=2A page=0f ea=bare book="ROR4 reg8" bookm="ROR4 mem8" diff=r:1,m00:1,d8:2,d16:2,dir:3 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q38) ROR4 is ROL4's routines with four words more (r8: 22, the qprobe runs; mem: twelve words before Z, the qprobe ror4m runs)"
    pop=modrm eac=r4r_r                     ; pop the ModR/M byte: register mode to the register path; a memory mode with a displacement calls its EA head
    ea=BI ra=BASE rb=INDEX                  ; the EA's add into the address register
    rl=1 bi alt                             ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P C: the ModR/M byte released; the commit word
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) Y: the request word (posted three words later)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR wid=BYTE                       ; post the byte's read (Y + 3)
    f ra=AW wid=BYTE alu=R4 ax=OPR ay=RA    ; D: F: the digit rotate (SIGMA the byte, tmpc the new AL)
    wr=AW wid=BYTE ws=TC                    ; AL written
    open call=w11                           ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) twelve words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 11)
    d1=OPRW s1=SIG bus=MEMW wid=BYTE        ; Z: the byte into the write datum; post the write (thirteen words after the datum: the model's twelve)
    e ro bi                                 ; E: G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)
r4r_r: open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) a word with no act
    rl=1                                    ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) P: the ModR/M byte released (the third word)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bi alt                                  ; (qprobe round 12, Q38) C: the commit word
    rb=RM ra=AW wid=BYTE alu=R4 ax=RB ay=RA ; the register and AL: the digit rotate
    wr=AW wid=BYTE ws=TC                    ; AL written
    wr=RM wid=BYTE ws=SIG                   ; the register written (F5b: after AL: with AL the operand, the operand's result stays, silicon f5r rot4al)
    open call=w10                           ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, Q38) eleven words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 10)
    e ro                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (N: fourteen words after the commit word)
